  "implemented": [
    "Separate sealed child User send command uses expectedRevision/body and trusted editor; exact Thread is an internal field covered by command identity, not accepted by deserialization",
    "Original SingleChat send/CAS/source/quote/consume/admit algorithm is shared through a sealed owner; legacy entry points still select only single_chat and work without delegation tables",
    "Child send reads its first owned attempt Runtime, validates frozen child role and Runtime identity, revalidates that installation/model/permission snapshot through the existing rebind resolver, and reapplies the same child policy exactly once",
    "New child User Run uses the frozen child workspace, delegation_user invocation, delegation_child_v1 policy, no business Task, zero public boundary and its own responsibility/Turn/message; original delegation_attempt is unchanged",
    "Original attempt-tree cleanup/recovery and prepared/unknown input fences are checked before source preparation and again in the command transaction; active User Run currently rejects while FIFO admission remains pending",
    "Child routing validates the User message before Run insert; same transaction links the new Run to that exact message, consumes the draft and stores quotes, with complete rollback on injected insertion failure",
    "Child CurrentInput accepts attachment-only User messages only with stored own source refs; initial tasks and resume messages remain nonempty and preserve their original checks"
  ],
